What are Ceria Slurries?
Ceria slurries are precision polishing compounds composed of cerium oxide (CeO₂) nanoparticles suspended in specialized liquid media. These formulations play a critical role in chemical mechanical planarization (CMP) processes for semiconductor fabrication, particularly for achieving atomic-level surface flatness in shallow trench isolation (STI) and interlayer dielectric (ILD) applications. The particle size distribution, typically ranging from 30nm to 200nm, and chemical composition significantly influence their polishing selectivity and defect performance.
